title: Remove deprecated treasury spend_local and remove_approval
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Removed `spend_local` and `remove_approval` (deprecated by May 2025), plus the related public
    getters, and dropped the legacy drain loop from `spend_funds` along with its
    `on_initialize_proposals` benchmark and weight entries.

    The legacy `ProposalCount` / `Proposals` / `Approvals` storage now lives behind
    `migration::legacy` aliases and is cleared by the new
    `migration::migrate_legacy_proposals::Migration`. That migration pays approved proposals out of
    the pot, refunds every proposer's bond and then deletes the legacy storage, doing in one
    upgrade what `spend_funds` previously did once per spend period. If the pot cannot cover an
    approved proposal, the migration defers it, logs a warning naming the index and amount, and
    keeps the legacy storage. **Before enacting the upgrade, a chain whose pot cannot cover an
    approved proposal must pay it out manually, fund the pot, or remove the approval: once this
    migration leaves the runtime `Migrations` tuple, deferred entries are orphaned with no code
    path left.** It is wired into the Rococo, Asset Hub Westend, Collectives Westend and
    kitchensink runtimes.

    `MaxApprovals` stays because the bounties pallet bounds its own `BountyApprovals` queue with it.
crates:
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: major
- name: collectives-westend-runtime
  bump: major
- name: rococo-runtime
  bump: major
- name: pallet-bounties
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-child-bounties
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-tips
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-treasury
  bump: major
